  <section>
    <h2>Why the official route stops most people</h2>
    <p>Telegram does have a real cash-out system, but it was designed for monetisation, not for individuals unloading a balance. Four conditions have to be met at once:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>You must have earned the Stars</strong>: through paid posts, paid reactions, tips, or sales inside your bot or Mini App. Stars you purchased do not qualify.</li>
      <li><strong>You need a Fragment account</strong>, which means connecting a TON wallet.</li>
      <li><strong>You wait 21 days.</strong> Telegram holds earned Stars for a fixed period before they can be converted.</li>
      <li><strong>You still end up holding TON</strong>, not money. To get som you then need a crypto exchange, usually with KYC on a foreign platform.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>For someone in Uzbekistan, the last step is the real wall. Buying and selling TON from an Uzbek bank card is awkward, the rate moves several percent in a day, and exchange fees eat into whatever you were trying to recover.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What about people who offer to buy your Stars?</h2>
    <p>Because the official route is closed to most users, you will see accounts and groups offering to "buy" Stars for cash. These deals happen outside Telegram's rules and carry real risk:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>They usually ask you to <strong>send the Stars first</strong> and promise to pay afterwards. Often the money never arrives.</li>
      <li>Telegram <strong>does not reverse</strong> Stars transfers, so there is no way to get them back.</li>
      <li>Some pretend to be a well-known shop. Always check through the shop's official channel or bot.</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>StarsJoy does not buy Stars from users.</strong> If someone offers to buy your Stars in StarsJoy's name, it has nothing to do with us.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Never share your login details</h2>
    <p>No genuine withdrawal of any kind needs your password, your SMS login code or your 2FA password. If someone asks for those, they are not processing a payout, they are taking your account.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>When cashing out is the wrong move</h2>
    <p>If you are holding Stars you intend to spend inside Telegram anyway, there is nothing to cash out. Stars do not expire and do not lose value sitting in your balance, so there is no pressure to move them. Use them for gifts, reactions, bots and Mini Apps.</p>
    <p>If you are a creator earning meaningful volume, the official Fragment route is worth setting up despite the friction: it scales, and the 21-day wait only bites once.</p>
  </section>

